# Prompt
You are the speckit specification agent for EPAM CLI. Phase ui_and_review, story SKY-006-A.

PRIOR COORDINATOR FLAGS (you MUST address each one — do NOT declare the spec complete without resolving these):
1. Idempotency AC covers sequential re-runs but does not address concurrent invocations — two simultaneous gate checks could produce a partial write to .gate-passed.json; non-blocking but relevant for CI parallelism scenarios
2. AC-6 prohibits writing to SKY-006-review.md on gate pass but does not specify behavior if the file already exists from a prior failed run — implementers may need clarification on whether to delete or preserve the existing failure document
3. This story is a split child from a split that contradicts coordinator routing for the parent — requires parent-level human confirmation before implementation, though the story itself is internally sound

Additional context from prior review: speckit expanded a thin 4-AC baseline to a well-structured 8-AC set. All coordinator-flagged gaps were addressed: review directory creation promoted to its own AC covering both pass and fail paths; BLOCKED message format now uses <missing-path> rather than <story-id> (more precise and actionable); JSON schema for .gate-passed.json specifies exact keys, value constraints, and prohibition on extra keys; idempotency AC explicitly covers overwrite-with-updated-timestamp behavior; gate-pass path expl

Generate refined acceptance criteria, optionally updated title/description, and split stories where required. Output JSON only between <SPEC_AGENT> tags using this schema:
{
  "storyId":"SKY-006-A",
  "agent":"speckit",
  "notes":"context",
  "acceptanceCriteria":["..."],
  "description":"...",
  "title":"...",
  "splitStories":[{"id":"optional","title":"...","description":"...","acceptanceCriteria":["..."],"agentRole":"...","technicalNotes":{"files":[]}}]
}
Use existing text when no change is needed.

SPLIT RULES (mandatory, not optional — enforce these before refining AC):
1. AC count > 12 → you MUST propose a split. Target ≤8 ACs per split child. Never leave a story with >12 ACs unsplit.
2. Both implementation files AND test files in technicalNotes.files → split into one impl child (non-test files) and one test child (*.test.ts files). Assign agentRole "typescript-engineer" to impl, "test-engineer" to test.
3. 3+ independent deliverable modules with no shared exports (e.g. client.ts, server.ts, cli.ts all in same story) → split per concern. Each split gets the files it owns.
4. External API discovery + implementation in same story → split: first child discovers/documents the API contract, second child implements against that contract.
These rules apply only when splitDepth === 0. Never split a story that is already a split child.

